# Bash hooks must check out with LF: under core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone
# otherwise gets CRLF scripts, and Git Bash fails on the \r characters.
*.sh text eol=lf
# The mutation ledger is parsed line-anchored by scripts/mutation-clock-check.sh.
# Git Bash and ubuntu-latest tolerate CRLF there (their awk/grep drop the CR),
# so this is belt-and-braces for the one setup that would not: a Linux
# toolchain reading a CRLF working tree (WSL, container bind mounts).
*.md text eol=lf
# scripts/practice_review_rollup.selftest.js extracts a source block out of the
# workflow by line-anchored markers and evaluates it. CR bytes in that block
# survive into the evaluated source, so pin both files to LF rather than trusting
# a checkout's autocrlf setting.
claude/workflows/*.js text eol=lf
scripts/*.selftest.js text eol=lf
